public class HouseholdService {

    /**
     * Creates a single NPSP Household Account and associates all supplied contacts with it.
     * The first contact in the list becomes the household's primary contact.
     *
     * @param members  New contacts (no Id, no AccountId). Must not be null or empty.
     * @return         The Id of the newly created Household Account.
     * @throws IllegalArgumentException if members is null or empty.
     */
    public static Id createHousehold(List<Contact> members) {
        if (members == null || members.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException('members must not be null or empty');
        }

        // Insert the first contact without an AccountId.
        // NPSP's trigger handler detects a Contact with no AccountId and automatically
        // creates a Household Account (correct record type, auto-generated name/greeting),
        // then links the contact to it.
        Contact first = members.get(0);
        insert first;

        // After the DML returns, the trigger has run synchronously and the
        // AccountId is populated on our in-memory record.
        Id householdId = first.AccountId;

        if (householdId == null) {
            throw new IllegalStateException(
                'Expected NPSP to auto-create a household for the primary contact, but AccountId was not set.'
            );
        }

        // Associate every remaining contact with the same household.
        if (members.size() > 1) {
            List<Contact> remaining = new List<Contact>();
            for (Integer i = 1; i < members.size(); i++) {
                members.get(i).AccountId = householdId;
                remaining.add(members.get(i));
            }
            insert remaining;
        }

        return householdId;
    }
}
```

**How it works:**

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|-------------|-----|
| 1. Validate | Throw `IllegalArgumentException` on null/empty | Requirement |
| 2. `insert first` (no AccountId) | NPSP's `NPE04__Trigger_Handler` fires on Contact insert, creates a Household Account (record type `Household`), generates the name/greeting from the contact, and sets `Contact.AccountId` | Lets NPSP own household creation—no hardcoded record-type Id, no manual `Account.Name`, guarantees the correct record type |
| 3. Read `first.AccountId` | The trigger ran synchronously during the DML, so the field is populated in our Apex variable | Gives us the single household to attach the rest of the family to |
| 4. Set `AccountId` on the rest, bulk insert | All remaining contacts join the same household; NPSP's trigger updates the household name to reflect the full family | One household, no orphans |

